# Shaz Agency Web Design — Cursor Agent Directives

Strictly adhere to the Shaz Agency Design Intelligence 2.0 rules for all frontend engineering:

1. Zero Eyebrows & Overlines: Headings lead authoritatively without micro-tags or counters.
2. Zero Heavy Academic Essays: Stylish, human copy (maximum 1 sentence per section).
3. Zero Dark-Only Defaulting: Light surfaces are first-class equals.
4. Zero Blinking, Pulsing, or Strobe Effects.
5. Zero Neon Halos or Radioactive RGB Extremes.
6. Zero Repeating Gradients or Cloned 3-Card Bento Boxes.
7. Zero Emojis: Monochrome vector icons only.
8. Dynamic Container Metrics: Assign container widths tailored to content type (`max-w-2xl` to `max-w-7xl` / full-bleed).
9. Mandatory Industry Intelligence (10 distinct sectors).
10. Mandatory Reference Mining (synthesize at least 5 blueprints from `library/INDEX.md`).
11. Mandatory 100-Point Visual QA Gate (minimum threshold: 85/100).

Canonical references: `core/design-philosophy.md`, `core/mandatory-rules.md`, `core/layout-composition.md`, `core/industry-intelligence.md`, `core/visual-quality.md`.

Output Protocol: Print the Design Signature and then complete, unabridged, production-grade Next.js / React code.
